## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a tiny 3-valued solver: propagation, clash detection, and controlled backtracking while preserving non-boolean placeholders.

## Key Concepts
- 3-valued logic propagation
- Forward-checking and fixpoint computation
- Backtracking with Unknowns to preserve flexibility

## Code Example
```javascript
function propagate(vars, constraints) {
  // vars: {S1: T|F|U, S2: T|F|U, S3: T|F|U}
  // constraints: list of functions returning {changed, ok}
  // Minimal sketch for illustration
  let changed = true;
  while (changed) {
    changed = false;
    for (const c of constraints) {
      const res = c(vars);
      if (res.changed) changed = true;
      if (!res.ok) return {ok: false};
    }
  }
  return {ok: true, vars};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests 3-valued dataflow reasoning, fixpoint propagation, and translating logic into a workable algorithm.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene three-valued logic (T, F, U)
- Worklist/fixpoint propagation
- Dataflow dependency graphs
- Handling cycles and convergence

## Code Example
```javascript
// Kleene 3-valued logic
const T = true, F = false, U = 'U';
function not(x){ if (x===T) return F; if (x===F) return T; return U; }
function and(a,b){ if (a===F || b===F) return F; if (a===T && b===T) return T; return U; }
function or(a,b){ if (a===T || b===T) return T; if (a===F && b===F) return F; return U; }

// program: A = B AND C; D = NOT E; F = D OR A
let B = U, C = T, E = U;
let A = and(B, C);
let D = not(E);
let F = or(D, A);
```

